  "notes": "The traditional reading is だいたい, but the reading だいがえ has become common in spoken Japanese. Both are accepted, though だいたい remains standard in formal and written contexts. Not to be confused with the adverb {大体|だいたい} (roughly, approximately), which is a different word entirely.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {代替|だいたい}{案|あん} (alternative plan)\n- {代替|だいたい}{手段|しゅだん} (alternative means)\n- {代替|だいたい}{品|ひん} (substitute product)\n- {代替|だいたい}エネルギー (alternative energy)\n- {代替|だいたい}{交通|こうつう} (substitute transportation)",
